---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Design with intention">
  <section class="hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Before you commit to a wall</span>
    <h1>Know how a room feels <em>before it exists.</em></h1>
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p>Most floor plans are a guess dressed up as a decision. House Designer turns a rough sketch into a space you can walk through and question — so you catch the cramped hallway on screen, not after the framing is up.</p>
      <div><a class="button" href="/contact">Build your first plan ↗</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="plan-mark" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </section>
  <section class="cards" aria-label="Product highlights">
    <article class="card"><span class="number">01 / DRAW</span><h3>Think in plans</h3><p>Sketch walls and rooms on a grid that keeps every proportion honest, before you second-guess it later.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><span class="number">02 / SEE</span><h3>Walk it through</h3><p>Step from a flat plan into a 3D walkthrough and see how the light and the layout actually feel.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><span class="number">03 / SHARE</span><h3>Make it legible</h3><p>Send a link, not a PDF. Everyone reacts to the same plan, the same view, the same decision.</p></article>
  </section>
</Layout>
